  Version 0.1.24 (2026-11-07)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * thermald is installed by the detection on Intel CPUs only, laptop or desktop (ORDER 43; found on a Ryzen 5 5600G): thermald prints "Unsupported cpu model or platform" and leaves on any other vendor without taking its bus name, so its unit failed at every boot, and sparky-stereo-hardware-support no longer depends on it. Before this version the detection added it for an Intel laptop and the metapackage added it on every machine, so an Intel desktop had it only through the metapackage and keeps it now through the detection (a machine that has it already keeps it: nothing is removed)
  * The machines that have thermald from an image before this version are settled once, after the apt run (usr/lib/sparky-stereo-hardware/thermald-manual, run by the postinst and by dpkg's post-invoke hook; inside an apt run it starts sparky-stereo-hardware-thermald-manual.service without waiting, which waits for the run to end because apt rewrites its state file at the end of a run). On an Intel CPU thermald is marked manually installed ("Intel machines keep it": `apt autoremove` would otherwise list it once the metapackage stops depending on it). On another CPU an automatically installed thermald that no installed package needs is removed (`apt-get remove`, configuration kept) and the journal says why. A thermald marked manual is left exactly as the person made it, even where it cannot run (Daniel, 2026-11-07: "If manually installed leave it, maybe a intel user is planning a migration"). A stamp (/var/lib/sparky-stereo-hardware/thermald-manual) makes it run once; ORDER 363b's pattern, without its problem record
  * NVIDIA's nvidia-imex is left alone: no package of the edition installs it (the open and the 580 stacks leave it out; only NVIDIA's own nvlink5 depends on it), so any copy is the person's
  * Tests: tests/detection.py gains an Intel desktop, an AMD laptop and a vendor that is neither (and the fixtures with an Intel CPU gain thermald); tests/thermald-manual.sh runs the step for Intel and AMD, automatic and manual, in a container; lists/tests/cpu-vendor-services-test.py keeps thermald, nvidia-imex and urfkill out of every image list

