  Version 0.1.23 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * After Hardware Setup switches NVIDIA stacks (the open modules and 615 to the 580 driver, or back), the previous stack's own leftovers go and the run says which (ORDER 390; Daniel, 2026-10-07: "we don't grow so fast, and when grow self prune", and never a general `apt autoremove`, which on his host would remove CUDA). Measured in clean containers: after a switch to 580, firmware-nvidia-gsp 615.71.09-2 stayed installed beside the 580 user space; after a switch to 615, libnvidia-egl-wayland1 and libwayland-server0 stayed. They are the packages the previous stack's own packages needed, that nothing needs now and that apt would autoremove; packages that were already unneeded before the switch, packages nobody installed for the NVIDIA stack, and everything the person installed stay. The removal is simulated first and must remove exactly these; if it would remove anything else, or apt fails, nothing more is removed and the run says so (two new messages, LOCAL59 and LOCAL60, in the nine languages)
  * The switch from NVIDIA's 580 driver to the open modules works: the setup looked for the module with apt's candidate, and while the 580 lock is installed it pins nvidia-kernel-open-dkms-stereo3d at -1, so apt had no candidate and the setup stopped with "apt finds no nvidia-kernel-open-dkms-stereo3d" (measured in a clean container with 0.1.22: the 580 driver stayed, nothing else changed). It now reads every version the sources offer; the lock install that follows replaces the 580 lock

